---
title: Baked mac and cheese
servings: 8
tags: [american, vegetarian]
cuisine: american
source: Adapted from Creamy Baked Macaroni and Cheese in tdstein/recipes (MIT), https://github.com/tdstein/recipes/blob/main/recipes/Creamy%20Baked%20Macaroni%20and%20Cheese.cook
---

Heat the oven to 350°F.

Boil the @dried pasta{1%lb}(elbow macaroni) in a #large pot{} of well-salted water until just
past al dente. Drain.

Set the empty pot over medium heat and melt the @unsalted butter{1/2%cup}. Let
it bubble ~{2%minutes}, whisking now and then, until it goes quiet.

Whisk in the @all-purpose flour{1/2%cup} and cook ~{1%minute} until smooth.

Whisk in the @whole milk{6%cup}. Turn the heat to high and bring to a simmer,
whisking all the time, then drop to low and simmer ~{3%minutes}, until it
lightly coats a spoon. It should still be fairly loose. Take the pot off the
heat.

Add the @cheddar cheese{1%lb}(extra-sharp, shredded),
@processed cheese{8%oz}(the soft melting loaf, cubed),
@Pecorino Romano{4%oz}(grated), @mustard powder{1/2%tsp},
@onion powder{1/4%tsp}, a pinch of @cayenne pepper{}, and @salt{} and
@black pepper{}. Whisk until melted and smooth.

Stir in the macaroni, breaking up any clumps, until every piece is coated. Taste
for seasoning.

Scrape into a #9x13-inch baking dish{} and bake ~{15%minutes}, until bubbling at
the edges. Serve straight away.
